Z||000000||burdell1||09-23-1999||11:15 AM||||Last winter i had problems with my heater fan not kicking in right away. I would turn it on and a few minutes later (the time would vary) it would kick in. It does it during the summer too, but I live in Minnesota and I only really care about the heater. Any ideas on why? Also, whenever I have the defrosters on, they only blow out of part of the vents not all the way across.||||reg||5
Z||000002||Greg Piet||09-23-1999||11:43 AM||||This reminded me!<BR>my heater does not seem to work.<BR>when telling it to heat, I hear doors opening/closing, but no heat.<BR>There is no leaking from the heater core.<BR>Apparently the previous owner used the magical radiator goop to try to fix a shot radiator.  My guess is that the heater core is filled/clogged with that goop.  Is that an  accurate guess?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||mwbackus||09-23-1999||12:31 PM||||Burdell : sounds like your blower motor is about ready to go south on ya..<P>Greg :  Good guess!  That garbage is responsible for more blown motors than just about any dump in quicky fix junk on the market.  The last thing one needs is a clogged coolant passage on a V6 head. I would probably just replace the heater core, but be sure to do a back flush to help rid your system of that gunk!<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||09-23-1999||03:06 PM||||Burdell 1 I had a similar promlem on my 85 turned out to be flakey terminals on the blower motor wire. Try wiggling the wire in the spare tire compartment and see what happens.||||reg||1
Z||000005||burdell1||01-03-2000||08:49 AM||||Phil, do you happen to know what colors the wires are? Does anybody out there have a blower motor for sale if it needs to be replaced? Are they easy to replace?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Phil||01-03-2000||09:39 AM||||Don't know the colors but the connector is easy enough to see. It is  to the left of the brake booster(as viewed from the front). I just looked at it again and there are two connectors: ground(African midnight-black) and hot (Hawaiian dawn-lavender).<p>[This message has been edited by Phil (edited 01-03-2000).]||||reg||1
